1
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:09,870
It's the truth that haunts us

2
00:06:07,741 --> 00:06:13,741
The River King is a drama, mystery, thriller film directed by Nick Willing.

3
00:09:11,612 --> 00:09:17,612
Abel Grey is sent to investigate the death of a boy from an
exclusive local school, who is found floating in the river.

4
00:12:15,483 --> 00:12:21,483
Fearing scandal, the school insists it was suicide.

5
00:15:19,354 --> 00:15:25,354
But after discovering from the boy's girlfriend, Carlin, that he was being badly bullied, Abel suspects that a dangerous
schoolboy initiation has gone horribly wrong and he secretly solicits the help of a sympathetic teacher, Betsy.

6
00:18:23,225 --> 00:18:29,225
He is warned off the investigation by his boss, as the school is a
generous benefactor to the Police benevolent fund.

7
00:21:27,096 --> 00:21:33,096
Abel, however, cannot let the case go, not only because his own brother committed suicide years before, but also it
seems that the spirit of the dead boy is leaving them clues as to what really happened that night.

8
00:24:30,967 --> 00:24:36,967
Abel Grey, played by Edward Burns.

9
00:27:34,838 --> 00:27:40,838
Betsy Chase, played by Jennifer Ehle.

10
00:30:38,709 --> 00:30:44,709
Joey Tosh, played by John Kapelos.

11
00:33:42,580 --> 00:33:48,580
Carlin Leander, played by Rachelle Lefevre.

12
00:36:46,451 --> 00:36:52,451
Joey's Son, played by Bruce Murphy.

13
00:39:50,322 --> 00:39:56,322
Eric Herman, played by Julian Rhind-Tutt.

14
00:42:54,193 --> 00:43:00,193
King Kong is a 2005 epic monster film directed,
co-written, produced by Peter Jackson.

15
00:45:58,064 --> 00:46:04,064
It is the ninth entry in the King Kong franchise and the second remake of the
1933 film of the same title, the first being the 1976 remake.

16
00:49:01,935 --> 00:49:07,935
The film stars Naomi Watts, Jack Black, Adrien Brody, Thomas Kretschmann, Colin
Hanks, Jamie Bell, and Andy Serkis as the motion capture of Kong.

17
00:52:05,806 --> 00:52:11,806
Set in 1933, it follows the story of an ambitious and unscrupulous filmmaker who tricks
his cast and hired ship crew into travelling to mysterious Skull Island.

18
00:55:09,677 --> 00:55:15,677
There they encounter various prehistoric creatures and a legendary giant
gorilla known as Kong, whom they capture and take to New York City.

19
00:58:13,548 --> 00:58:19,548
Development began in early 1995, when Universal Pictures approached
Jackson to direct the remake of the original 1933 film.

20
01:01:17,419 --> 01:01:23,419
The project stalled in early 1997, as several ape and giant monster-related films were under production
at the time and Jackson planned to direct The Lord of the Rings film series instead.

21
01:04:21,290 --> 01:04:27,290
As the first two films in the Rings trilogy became commercially successful, Universal went back to Jackson in early
2003, expressing interest in restarting development on the project, to which Jackson eventually agreed.

22
01:07:25,161 --> 01:07:31,161
Filming for King Kong took place in New Zealand
from September 2004 to March 2005.

23
01:10:29,032 --> 01:10:35,032
It was the most expensive film ever produced at the time of its release, as its budget
climbed from an initial $150 million to a then record-breaking $207 million.

24
01:13:32,903 --> 01:13:38,903
King Kong premiered at New York City on 5 December 2005, and was theatrically released
in New Zealand on December 13 and in the United States on 14 December.

25
01:16:36,774 --> 01:16:42,774
The film received critical acclaim, and eventually appeared in several top ten lists for 2005; it was praised for the special effects,
performances, sense of spectacle and comparison to the 1933 original, though some criticisms were raised over its 3-hour runtime.

26
01:19:40,645 --> 01:19:46,645
It was a commercial success, grossing over $557 million, and became the fourth-highest-grossing film in
Universal Pictures history at that time and the fifth-highest-grossing film of 2005.

27
01:22:44,516 --> 01:22:50,516
It also generated $100 million in DVD sales upon its
home video release in March 2006.

28
01:25:48,387 --> 01:25:54,387
It won three Academy Awards for Best Sound Editing, Best
Sound Mixing and Best Visual Effects.

29
01:28:52,258 --> 01:28:58,258
A tie-in video game was released alongside the film, which
also became a commercial and critical success.

30
01:31:56,129 --> 01:32:02,129
The tone is intense and lighthearted and emotional.
